+## Independent evidence
+
+Fresh arithmetic (inline Python, no agent/project code reused), at `n=20,50,100`:
+naive MITM midpoint count `(n^2)^{d/2}`, `d=n*ceil(log2 n)`, gives
+`log2 = d*log2 n = Theta(n log2^2 n)` — the same exponent as full DFS
+( verified: 432 vs 374, 1693 vs 1593, 4651 vs 4414 against `n log2^2 n` ),
+far above an `O(n log n)` target. `F(P) in {0,...,n*ceil(log2 n)}` so `O(n log n)`
+values; e.g. `2^1104` barrier states collapse into `<=701` F-values at `n=100`.
+
+**Theorem 1** (compact sufficient statistic ⇔ P-membership) is correct but
+definitional: a poly-time-computable `h` with poly-time decoding of `F(P)`,
+applied at the root, computes `S(n)` in poly time (⇒ SORT-BOUND-U ∈ P); the
+converse takes `h=F`. Already implied by the project's "Realistic outcomes"
+and `research-plan.md`. Out of scope, changes no classification.
+
+**Theorem 2** (barrier measures isomorphism refinement; F collapses it) is
